{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.descRun_eq_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.descRun_eq_cons","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.lean#L86-L97","doc":"**A block's word begins with its top index.**\n\nTakes `j ≤ i` as a hypothesis rather than deriving it, so it is usable the\nmoment the threshold-to-pointwise bridge lands and is not blocked on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.descRun_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.descRun_le","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.lean#L77-L84","doc":"**Every letter of a block is at most the block's top index.**\n\nThis is the half of the block structure the δ rule consumes: an earlier block\nwhose top is `≤ k-2` has *all* its letters `≤ k-2`, hence all far from `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.elems_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.elems_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**`elems` is strictly increasing** — inherited from `List.finRange` through\n`Sublist`, with no sorting step and no sortedness proof of its own. That is the\nwhole reason `elems` is a `filter` rather than a `Finset.sort`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.mem_elems","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.mem_elems","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebWordBlocks.lean#L67-L69","doc":"`elems` lists exactly the members of `s`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}